.\" M4KK1 4P1 - m4sh.1
.TH M4SH 1 "2026-07-22" "M4KK1 1.0" "M4KK1 User Commands"
.SH NAME
m4sh \- M4KK1 Shell, interactive command-line interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B m4sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
M4SH is the init process (PID 1) of M4KK1, providing an interactive command-line environment with command execution, pipelines, redirection, environment variables, command history, and Tab completion.
.SH LINE EDITING
.TP
.B Character keys
Append to command buffer
.TP
.B Backspace / 0x7F
Delete last character
.TP
.B Enter / 0x0D
Execute command
.TP
.B Tab
Command name completion
.TP
.B Up / Esc [ A
Previous history entry
.TP
.B Down / Esc [ B
Next history entry
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Cancel current line
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Exit shell on empty line
.SH OPERATORS
.TP
.B \;
Sequential execution
.TP
.B &&
Execute next on success
.TP
.B \|\|
Execute next on failure
.TP
.B \|
Pipeline
.SH QUOTING
.TP
.B \'...\'
Literal, no variable expansion
.TP
.B \"...\"
Reserved, supports \e" \e\e \e$ escapes
.TP
.B \e
Escape next character
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Up to 16 variables, 128 bytes each. Export: export VAR=value. Expand: $VAR or ${VAR}.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR cat (1),
.BR grep (1),
.BR echo (1)
